{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"Main_Section": "**9. ARTICLE 5(1)(H) AI ACT - REAL-TIME REMOTE BIOMETRIC IDENTIFICATION (RBI) SYSTEMS FOR LAW ENFORCEMENT PURPOSES**", "Sub_Section": "**9.1. Rationale and objectives**", "Letter_Section": "**_c) Reference database_**", "source": "clean_eu_proh_ai_act.md"}, "page_content": "#### **_c) Reference database_**  \n- (309) Identification is not possible without a reference database containing biometric data for comparison purposes. Thus, the existence of a reference database is **indispensable** to perform the comparison for identification purposes.<sup>189</sup>  \nFor example, in the case of missing persons, the Schengen Information System<sup>190</sup> database could be used as the reference database for facial recognition purposes (once operational).", "type": "Document"}}